{"page":450,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.37889,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"436 Chapter 7: Integrals and Transcendental Functions"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09343,"w":0.59307,"h":0.02815,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"surrounding medium. This observation is called Newton’s Law of Cooling, although it applies to warming as well."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.12413,"w":0.58896,"h":0.02815,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"If H is the temperature of the object at time t and HS is the constant surrounding tem- perature, then the differential equation is"},{"x":0.55161,"y":0.16297,"w":0.01997,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dH"},{"x":0.55528,"y":0.1695,"w":0.35697,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dt = -k(H - HS). (8)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.20019,"w":0.24134,"h":0.01498,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"If we substitute y for (H - HS), then"},{"x":0.46495,"y":0.2219,"w":0.01543,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dy"},{"x":0.46631,"y":0.22435,"w":0.04897,"h":0.02728,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dt = d"},{"x":0.50486,"y":0.22435,"w":0.12314,"h":0.02728,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dt(H - HS) = dH"},{"x":0.61169,"y":0.22435,"w":0.05128,"h":0.02728,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dt - d"},{"x":0.65254,"y":0.23155,"w":0.04254,"h":0.02008,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dt(HS)"},{"x":0.48778,"y":0.25505,"w":0.03705,"h":0.01999,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= dH"},{"x":0.50853,"y":0.26158,"w":0.30639,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"dt - 0 HS is a constant."},{"x":0.48779,"y":0.28574,"w":0.03705,"h":0.01999,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= dH"},{"x":0.48779,"y":0.30023,"w":0.27518,"h":0.03005,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"dt = -k(H - HS) Eq. (8)"},{"x":0.48779,"y":0.33832,"w":0.30664,"h":0.01432,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"= -ky. H - HS = y"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.35158,"w":0.58893,"h":0.04009,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Now we know that the solution of dy>dt = -ky is y = y0e-kt, where y(0) = y0. Substitut- ing (H - HS) for y, this says that"},{"x":0.53036,"y":0.40617,"w":0.38189,"h":0.01655,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"H - HS = (H0 - HS)e-kt, (9)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.4304,"w":0.59295,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"where H0 is the temperature at t = 0. This equation is the solution to Newton’s Law of Cooling."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.47925,"w":0.59297,"h":0.04519,"fs":0.01407,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 6 A hard-boiled egg at 98°C is put in a sink of 18°C water. After 5 min, the egg’s temperature is 38°C. Assuming that the water has not warmed appreciably, how much longer will it take the egg to reach 20°C?"},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.53893,"w":0.58895,"h":0.04434,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"Solution We find how long it would take the egg to cool from 98°C to 20°C and sub- tract the 5 min that have already elapsed. Using Equation (9) with HS = 18 and H0 = 98, the egg’s temperature t min after it is put in the sink is"},{"x":0.4953,"y":0.58834,"w":0.27451,"h":0.01795,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"H = 18 + (98 - 18)e-kt = 18 + 80e-kt."},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.61584,"w":0.38987,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"To find k, we use the information that H = 38 when t = 5:"},{"x":0.54138,"y":0.63766,"w":0.12226,"h":0.01467,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"38 = 18 + 80e-5k"},{"x":0.53317,"y":0.65553,"w":0.05715,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"e-5k = 1"},{"x":0.53105,"y":0.68622,"w":0.07404,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"-5k = ln1"},{"x":0.59691,"y":0.69257,"w":0.06881,"h":0.02068,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"4 = -ln 4"},{"x":0.48879,"y":0.71691,"w":0.03984,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"k = 1"},{"x":0.52046,"y":0.72327,"w":0.22713,"h":0.02084,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"5 ln 4 = 0.2 ln 4 (about 0.28)."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.75276,"w":0.59303,"h":0.01467,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The egg’s temperature at time t is H = 18 + 80e-(0.2ln4)t. Now find the time t when"},{"x":0.32424,"y":0.76931,"w":0.05706,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"H = 20:"},{"x":0.56379,"y":0.78345,"w":0.15308,"h":0.01467,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"20 = 18 + 80e-(0.2ln4)t"},{"x":0.50837,"y":0.79936,"w":0.10429,"h":0.01795,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"80e-(0.2ln4)t = 2"},{"x":0.52471,"y":0.82051,"w":0.09212,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"e-(0.2ln4)t = 1"},{"x":0.60456,"y":0.83475,"w":0.01634,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"40"},{"x":0.50803,"y":0.84864,"w":0.12356,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"-(0.2ln4)t = ln 1"},{"x":0.61933,"y":0.85499,"w":0.08314,"h":0.02068,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"40 = -ln40"},{"x":0.57562,"y":0.87661,"w":0.15272,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"t = ln40 0.2ln4 ≈13 min."},{"x":0.3233,"y":0.90683,"w":0.593,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"The egg’s temperature will reach 20°C about 13 min after it is put in the water to cool. Since it took 5 min to reach 38°C, it will take about 8 min more to reach 20°C."}]}